abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v23.3 keeps everything in v23.2: CORE.md opens with what a
  functional world model is and follows one model of learning, read as a
  network, in eight steps, and formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean audits 96
  machine-checked results; no Lean module is added. It adds four pieces of
  work outside the core, each labelled where it stands. A working note
  compares two ways to charge for misfit in learning, counting wrong worlds
  and the log-loss of the actual world; an outside review reproduced every
  number, its corrections were accepted, and it judged that nothing
  mathematical is added. A feasibility study of the Ten Verbs Hypothesis, in
  one model written by the assistant, asks whether a task can tell ten
  proposed functions of learning apart; four outside reviews are kept, and
  it is closed as a feasibility study with a brief for an independent
  experiment. A working note reads OpenAI's published base-model perplexity
  curve through two of the author's January 2026 preprints on functional
  information, states five predictions with what would count against each,
  reports that one already fails a first check, and designs a study on open
  model checkpoints that has not been run. In the Yang–Mills working space,
  an attempt to prove that a quantity D(p) never decreases, which would make
  a crossing probability nondecreasing, gives a reformulation, two lemmas
  and a failed route, and no proof; the space still contains no mass-gap
  result. Retained from v23.2: the working note on what one turn of learning
  consists of, the creed's two draft sections and the legal concept note. No
  human expert has reviewed the additions of this release. DIALOGUE.md
  records how the author and an AI assistant build the model together, now
  in 54 entries. The release title uses ‘simulation of reality’ to mean the
  internal model through which a system experiences and acts in the world,
  not a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal verification
  establishes implications under explicit premises; empirical, causal,
  political and normative interpretations remain open. The original
  repository material is dual-licensed under CC BY 4.0 OR Apache-2.0 as
  documented in DUAL-LICENSING.md; CC BY 4.0 is supplied here as the single
  Zenodo archival metadata value because the GitHub-Zenodo metadata path
  accepts one license value.
